------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAP (web source → native)
------------------------------------------------------------
  useLocation() pathname change   → RouteSource emits RouteDescriptor(path,title); model
                                    keys announcements on `path` change (web [pathname] dep)
  document.title (usePageTitle)   → localized route title via RouteTitleResolver
                                    (String(localized:"route.<id>"), same as AppShell)
  firstRender guard (no announce) → first observation recorded silently → phase .idle
  if(!title) setMessage('')       → empty title clears the region → phase .silent
  '\u200B'.repeat(counter % 4)    → RouteAnnouncerPadding (increment-then-pad, mod 4) so a
                                    repeated title still re-speaks (defeats AT de-dup)
  100 ms settle setTimeout        → injectable scheduler seam (defaultDelayMs = 100)
  clearTimeout cleanup            → newer navigation cancels the in-flight announcement
  aria-live="polite" region       → AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(...).post()
                                    + a visually-hidden, navigable live-region element
  dedicated region (NOT useAnnouncer) → reproduced verbatim: this surface owns its own
                                    region so an imperative announcement cannot clobber it
                                    (the web source documents exactly this decision)

States reproduced = the web source's ACTUAL branches: idle (suppressed first render),
announcing (non-empty title), silent (empty title clears region). There is deliberately NO
loading/error/offline branch — the web source performs no data fetch (it reads a synchronous
local value off a router subscription), so those generic leaf states cannot occur here; the
honest, non-drifting state set is the three above. Every one renders (see Previews + the
visible inspector + the per-state projection tests).

